Key Empirical Findings:
The Invalidation of China-Price Parity: In critical categories—infant nutrition, active dermaceuticals, precision electronics, and European automotive sensors—customers actively distrust cheap alternatives. They pay a 25%–40% premium for verified UK provenance.
