Objective: Detect wrong variants, missing items, or transit damage in the UK before international freight costs are incurred.
The 5-Point Inspection Checklist:
Tamper Seal Integrity: Check that factory seals on infant formula tins, cosmetics, and electronics are 100% intact.
Specification Verification: Cross-reference item SKU, colorway, size, and model number against customer order request.
Shelf-Life / Expiry Check: Infant formula and vitamins must possess a minimum of 12 months shelf-life before expiration.
Structural Packaging Condition: Reject any tin with denting, punctured foil, or leaking liquid seals.
Electrical Specification: Verify 230V / 50Hz rating and standard UK 3-pin plug (Type G).
Visual Customer Artifact: 4 high-resolution photos (front, rear, tamper seal, batch/expiry code) are uploaded to the customer portal and triggered via WhatsApp notification.
SOP-03: Exception Handling, Discrepancies & Stockouts
Objective: Provide automated, transparent solutions when products are out of stock or arrive defective.
Scenarios & Resolutions:
Scenario A (UK Retailer Stockout): If the primary retailer goes out of stock before purchase, the system checks approved secondary suppliers. If price difference is 
, KoraBridge absorbs the difference. If 
, the customer is sent an instant 1-click approval via WhatsApp to accept the alternative or receive a 100% instant Naira refund.
Scenario B (Defective Delivery in UK): If an item arrives damaged at the London hub, it is rejected immediately under the UK Consumer Rights Act 2015. A merchant replacement is ordered the same day; the customer receives an automated alert with updated delivery ETA.
Scenario C (Customer Cancellation): Permitted with 100% refund prior to UK purchase. Post-purchase cancellations incur a £3.50 retailer domestic return fee + £10.00 restocking charge; remainder is refunded in Naira.
