Objective: Minimize volumetric air freight charges and eliminate transit pilferage.
Protocol:
Volumetric Down-Sizing: UK retailers routinely dispatch small items in oversized cardboard boxes filled with paper padding. The operator reboxes goods into form-fitting double-walled corrugated cartons, saving an average of 35%–45% on volumetric freight bills.
Pilferage Protection: Every parcel is sealed using branded, tamper-evident security tape printed with sequential serial numbers. If the tape is slit by cargo handlers, the words "OPENED / VOID" appear across the carton surface.
