Cryptographic Webhook Security (Paystack HMAC-SHA512)
Payment confirmation bypasses browser callbacks completely. The server validates the raw binary payload using HMAC-SHA512 against the environment secret:
If x-paystack-signature does not match in constant-time comparison (crypto.timingSafeEqual), the request is rejected with 401 Unauthorized. Upon validation, an idempotent transaction row is inserted; duplicate webhook events are acknowledged with 200 OK without triggering duplicate order sourcing.
4. Security, Compliance, & Anti-Fraud Engine
Anti-Fraud & Card-Testing Prevention:
Rate limiting on checkout initialization (max 3 payment attempts per IP/account per hour).
High-value order threshold: Any transaction over ₦1,500,000 (£750) requires Tier 2 verification (matching customer phone, BVN check, or ID document) prior to UK retail dispatch.
Data Protection & Privacy:
Compliance with both UK GDPR / Data Protection Act 2018 (for UK operations) and the Nigeria Data Protection Act (NDPA 2023) for consumer data.
PII (delivery address, telephone numbers) stored with AES-256 encryption at rest; payment card details are never handled or stored directly (delegated to PCI-DSS Level 1 Paystack/Flutterwave).
Audit Trail & Integrity:
All state transitions in the order lifecycle are immutable and append-only in order_audit_logs.
